ters validate every selected input site in dependency order, erase proof fields, expose constructor-free copied results, preserve rejected caller graphs and recover on the next valid call. Closed Bool, String and Nat indices remain authenticated type metadata rather than host fields. The generated C/GMP, C++ multiprecision, C# BigInteger, Java BigInteger and Kotlin BigInteger records expose only proof-free payloads. Full packages validate all eight indexed inputs through the exact selected Lean constructors, preserve rejected caller values, recover on the next valid call and return all eight proof-free results. Standalone result-only packages expose the same results without checked-input metadata. Proof-only Witness crosses as a nominal empty carrier; C uses one non-semantic uint8_t storage byte solely to give the structure a legal nonzero size, while C++ uses an empty structure. Token keeps its Unit field, plain empty Marker remains an ordinary empty record, and Option presence, arrays, and the active or inactive Mark branches remain distinct. Full packages validate nullary checked constructors and exact rejection and recovery. Result-only packages project Lean-produced proof-erased values without input-constructor metadata."
